Package: teddy
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: agent daemon exposing a REST API to exec commands and transfer files
 Teddy is a small agent daemon written in Rust (Actix-web 4), deployable on
 Linux, macOS and Windows. It exposes a REST API to execute a command
 (single command, no shell), upload files via multipart form (up to 100 MB)
 and download files from the machine. Prometheus metrics are exposed on a
 dedicated port (:9000/metrics).
 .
 The /admin/* endpoints are protected by an Authorization header equal to
 Base64(user:password). Configuration lives in /etc/teddy/config.json
 (optional: sane defaults are built in). The systemd unit is installed but
 not enabled: set strong credentials in /etc/teddy/config.json first, then
 run "systemctl enable --now teddy". Never expose Teddy on an untrusted
 network: it is a remote-execution agent by design.
